#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area made of tightly placed bricks.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "rock floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area of rock and stone.  Looks stable enough to be mined "
"with the proper mining gear.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped stone floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A rough stone floor.  Its patterns constantly shift as if your mind can't "
"quite understand what it's really seeing.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, gray, rubbery material.  Can "
"support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, rubbery material.  Colored a "
"simple white.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "small rebar roof cage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A series of structural supports crafted from rebar in order to allow the "
"pouring of concrete for a more stable floor and roof support."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "junk metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A simple roof of rusty scrap metal bolted and wire-tied to a makeshift "
"frame.  Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  Hope you like the"
" sound of rain on corrugated metal.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "marble floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A smooth and flat flooring made of marble tiles.  Beautiful and expensive.  "
"Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "thick slag"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A thick layer of slag piled up and cooled here, knee high to a grown man."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "jagged slag"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "A thick, jagged layer of slag, cooled into spiky projections."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "thin slag"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A thin layer of slag coats the floor in rippling waves.  It has cooled "
"completely solid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper brood cap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A thin paper floor, protecting the pupating wasp larva until it's ready to "
"emerge."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "primitive floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "A timber floor and supports that can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance, covered by a canvas floor.  May support a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open air"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
