#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin carbine"
#. ~ Description of "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"A later produced and substantially shortened version of Imperial Russia's "
"original service rifle, this variant of the Mosin features a notably more "
"compact barrel and an integral side-folding bayonet.  Produced during the "
"latter days of the Second World War for the Soviet Union, the weapon "
"exhibits less overall stopping power than its full-length older brother "
"thanks to the former's stubbier barrel.  Despite the arm being somewhat "
"weaker than its forefather, the 7.62x54mm round that it chambers still packs"
" a hefty punch, whilst its smaller size helps to make the weapon wieldier."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"Developed by the Russian Empire prior to the onset of the First World War, "
"the Mosin is a bolt-action military battle rifle chambered for 7.62x54mm "
"rounds.  Powerful, unwieldy, and prolific across the world as military "
"surplus, this sizable rifle is a Soviet updated version of the venerable "
"Mosin."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Mosin battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "모신 전투소총"

