" down or pry walls or cabinets to gain access in case of a fire."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A socketed bronze axe with a work-hardened edge, tightly bound to the shaft "
"with cords."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "stone adze"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A stone adze, a primitive tool for smoothing or scraping wood objects."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "stone axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"A stone with a narrow edge affixed to a stick.  It can chop wood, but "
"requires much more effort than a modern axe."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid ""
"An axe designed for medieval warfare, the head secured to the haft with "
"langets.  Though formidable, it's lighter than the sort you'd use for "
"felling trees, and would make an inferior tool for that purpose."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "Marrying strap for a Halligan bar."
msgstr "할리건 바를 부착하는 스트랩입니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
