#. ~ Description of "ballistic Kevlar panel"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"16 layers of ballistic Kevlar sheets stacked and stitched together into a "
"soft, flexible panel.  Ballistic Kevlar is precision-made by machine and "
"features an extremely tight and uniform weave which cannot be replicated by "
"hand.  Given that the material isn't useful for cut-resistant applications "
"and relies on being stackeed in layers to function, there's no reason to try"
" and take it apart."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Kevlar plate"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A compressed panel of layered Kevlar fabric saturated with epoxy or other "
"adhesive to make it stiff as a board."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wool staple"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A natural cluster of wool fibers.  It could be processed into felt patches "
"or spun into yarn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fur patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized piece of preserved fur from an animal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "denim patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A palm-sized square of densely-woven cotton.  Denim is usually used for "
"making jeans, but the fabric is both tough and soft enough for a variety of "
"uses."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Kevlar patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A palm-sized square of loosely-woven Kevlar fabric.  This variety lacks in "
"ballistic protection, but would be great for making cut-resistant garments."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nylon patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized square of synthetic fabric."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "canvas patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A palm-sized square of tough canvas fabric.  It could be used to repair "
"items made of canvas or stitched into patchwork sheets for tailoring "
"projects."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "gambeson batting"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A pile of shredded fabric, dry grass, hair or other cheap materials which "
"could be used to stuff the fabric layers of a gambeson to create armor more "
"cheaply and easily than properly layering and quilting the entire product."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cured pelt"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A rolled-up animal hide which has been scraped of extraneous hair and flesh "
"and treated to prevent decay.  It still requires tanning to become usable "
"fur."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cured hide"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A rolled-up animal hide which has been scraped of extraneous hair and flesh "
"and treated to prevent decay.  It still requires tanning to become usable "
"leather."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "leather patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A roughly six-inch square patch of leather, could be used to repair clothing"
" and make smaller leather crafts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Nomex sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of Nomex synthetic fabric, suitable for making heat-resistant "
"clothing."
msgstr "노멕스 인조 섬유 천입니다. 열에 강한 의복을 만드는 데에 알맞습니다."

#. ~ Description of "denim sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of densely woven cotton.  Denim is usually used for making jeans, "
"but the fabric is both tough and soft enough for a variety of uses."
msgstr ""

